Link TCL.EXE with libc16 and libkitchen16 (docs/DESIGN.md, sections 4.2
and 12).

libc16 0.15 has everything Tiny Tcl calls but sscanf, environ and the
<dirent.h> functions; libkitchen16 0.02 has sprintf, fprintf,
vfprintf, strtod and the floating point helpers of wcc -fpc. With
TCL16_LIBC16 defined:

- tclInt.h and panic.c include <kitchen16.h> after libc16's headers,
  so that the formatted output and strtod have their __cdecl
  prototypes.
- tcldos.h includes Tcl16's "dosdir.h" (src/dosdir.c) for opendir,
  readdir and closedir, over _dos_findfirst and _dos_findnext.
- tclEnv.c keeps its own environ, made from the environment block
  TCL.EXE was started with (src/dosenv.c), and TclEnviron gives it to
  exec.

panic ends TCL.EXE with exit(255), the status Tcl16 documents for it
(docs/COMPATIBILITY.md, section 4), rather than abort(): libc16's abort
exits with 3, after a message of its own.

In every build, Tcl_ScanCmd calls Tcl16_Sscanf (src/scan.c), which scans
the formats Tcl_ScanCmd passes, in place of the C library's sscanf.

